WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.685
Alpine Linux upgraded GitLab twice

00:00:02.485 --> 00:00:04.771
after a critical fix shipped,

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.783
and stayed exposed for two weeks.

00:00:07.483 --> 00:00:09.185
The GitLab bug scores a

00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:10.536
maximum ten out of ten.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:12.596
On Thursday, CISA listed it

00:00:12.396 --> 00:00:13.396
as exploited.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.722
GitLab CI files can use

00:00:15.522 --> 00:00:18.457
regex patterns, which Ruby's built-in

00:00:18.257 --> 00:00:19.618
engine compiles.

00:00:19.658 --> 00:00:21.602
A crafted pattern triggers an

00:00:21.402 --> 00:00:23.279
overflow and runs commands on

00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:23.882
the server.

00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:26.398
GitLab patched only the Ruby

00:00:26.198 --> 00:00:27.870
inside its own packages.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.981
Custom builds kept the broken

00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:31.627
engine until Ruby's own fix

00:00:31.427 --> 00:00:33.124
on October twenty-third.

00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:35.308
On October thirteenth,

00:00:35.108 --> 00:00:37.197
Alpine installed a build briefly

00:00:36.997 --> 00:00:38.045
listed as fixed.

00:00:38.085 --> 00:00:40.240
Attacks began on the twentieth,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.724
and a second upgrade kept

00:00:41.524 --> 00:00:43.275
stock Ruby until a rebuild

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:44.489
on the twenty-seventh.

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:47.393
The attacks crashed GitLab's workers

00:00:47.193 --> 00:00:48.921
eight times in two days,

00:00:48.721 --> 00:00:51.004
and four got partway before failing.

00:00:51.554 --> 00:00:53.601
Alpine says the attack failed,

00:00:53.401 --> 00:00:54.986
but it cannot prove it,

00:00:54.786 --> 00:00:56.436
because a clean hit would

00:00:56.236 --> 00:00:57.228
leave no crash.

00:00:57.778 --> 00:00:59.624
Check your GitLab version,

00:00:59.424 --> 00:01:01.599
because nineteen point three point

00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:02.521
four is not fixed.

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:04.356
Custom builds also need a

00:01:04.156 --> 00:01:06.604
fixed Ruby and freshly pulled images.

00:01:07.154 --> 00:01:08.904
If you cannot patch yet,

00:01:08.704 --> 00:01:11.159
block anonymous access and untrusted

00:01:10.959 --> 00:01:12.710
writes to public projects.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.490
Then look for traces and

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:15.491
rotate secrets.

00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:17.895
Fixes increasingly live in a

00:01:17.695 --> 00:01:19.749
dependency, not in the product

00:01:19.549 --> 00:01:21.073
whose version you check.

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:22.520
Read the full story on

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.258
The Dispatch.

